BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  In the beginning, there was only the dry soil of the Void. Two spirits, Aethel and Solis, held) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (     seeds of life. Aethel chose to keep hers, fearful of the shifting winds. Her seeds remained) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (     stagnant, gray pebbles in a locked chest. Solis, however, walked to the edge of the chasm a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    nd cast his seeds across the expanse to Aethel. As they traveled, the air transformed them, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    tripling their potential through the magic of the chasm's breath. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  Aethel caught the bounty. She understood the weight of the gift. Recognizing the spirit of tru) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    st, she returned a portion of the harvest back to Solis. The return was not just a transacti) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    on; it was a weave, binding their fates. Where once there was dust, a forest grew, fed by th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    e constant cycle of giving and receiving. The spirits learned that holding onto one's grain ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    meant starving, but pouring it into the hands of another created a harvest that neither coul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    d achieve alone. In this realm, the multiplier of trust is the only currency that yields a g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    arden. To hold is to wither; to release is to flourish. Thus, the cycle of the chasm became ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    the law of the cosmos: give freely, return justly, and watch the world bloom.) Tj ET
