BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  In the Valley of Echoes, two spirits lived on opposite sides of a vast canyon. The Weaver held) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (     the silver thread, representing the initial gift, while the Merchant guarded the golden loo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    m, which possessed the power to multiply whatever was placed upon it. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  If the Weaver kept the thread, the canyon remained silent and barren. If the Weaver cast the t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    hread across the chasm, the Merchant would weave it into a brilliant tapestry, tripling its ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    worth. The Weaver often feared the Merchant might shroud the tapestry in secrecy, keeping th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    e entire bounty. Yet, the Merchant understood that if the thread never arrived, the loom wou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    ld remain cold and empty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  One day, the Weaver took a leap of faith and tossed the silver thread. The Merchant, recognizi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    ng the sanctity of this offering, did not hoard the silk. Instead, they returned a portion t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    o the Weaver, honoring the courage it took to trust. They realized that by acting in concert) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    , their prosperity grew beyond the canyon's limits. They held an unspoken pact: trust is the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (     loom, and reciprocity is the thread. They learned that the greatest return lies not in what) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (     one keeps, but in the enduring cycle of mutual grace.) Tj ET
