BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (  In the primordial era, the Great Sun and the Silent Earth existed in a cycle of eternal exchan) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (    ge. The Sun, possessing the radiant fire of creation, would cast its golden rays toward the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (    earth. This was the offering. If the Earth kept the warmth locked within its crust, the worl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    d stagnated, turning brittle and barren. But when the Earth opened its valleys to the light,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (     transforming the warmth into lush forests and flowing rivers, it sent back the vitality of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    life-the fragrant blossoms and the cool, damp mist.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  This was the Law of the Radiant Cycle: the Sun sent the fire, and the Earth returned the fruit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (    . There was no need for complex oaths, only the rhythmic pulse of giving and receiving. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    Sun never feared the void, knowing the Earth would answer in kind, and the Earth never feare) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    d the winter, knowing the Sun would return with the dawn. When a partner holds back, the for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    est withers; when both give fully, the garden flourishes beyond measure. True prosperity is ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    not found in what one hoards, but in the abundance generated by an unbroken chain of trust, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    where each partner honors the other's contribution as their own.) Tj ET
