BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  In the beginning, the world was a barren loom. The Weaver held five golden seeds, the raw pote) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ntial of existence. She met the Merchant at the crossroads of the void. "If I plant these in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (     your soil," the Weaver asked, "will you nurture them?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  The Merchant nodded, his hands calloused by trade. The Weaver cast her seeds across the divide) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    . As they touched the Merchant's garden, the magic of the earth tripled their value, turning) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (     five into fifteen, a golden bounty. The Weaver watched, her heart fluttering, wondering if ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    the Merchant would hoard the harvest or honor the bond.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  The Merchant stood before the abundance. Greed whispered to lock the gates, to claim the fifte) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    en for himself. But memory stirred-he recalled the Weaver's initial vulnerability, the risk ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    she had taken in a desolate land. He realized that reciprocity was the water that kept the s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    oil fertile. He gathered the gold and returned a generous portion to the Weaver, ensuring th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    at when the next season arrived, their dance would continue. They became the architects of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (     thriving cycle, proving that trust is not a weakness to be exploited, but a currency that g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    rows only when it is shared and returned in kind.) Tj ET
