BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  In the dawn of the world, two brothers, Sol and Luna, stood before the Great Well of Abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    . The Well demanded a gift to multiply its waters. Sol held five golden seeds. If he kept th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    em, they remained mere pebbles. If he cast them into the depths, they tripled in number, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (     he relied on Luna to share the bounty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  Sol cast his seeds into the dark water. The Well surged, returning fifteen golden grains. Luna) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    , standing at the edge, faced a choice. If he walked away, he would be rich for a moment, bu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    t the Well would grow cold, and the brothers would starve in the coming winter. Instead, Lun) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    a scooped up the grains and returned half to Sol, honoring the cycle of growth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  "We are but stewards of the flow," Luna whispered. Sol smiled, understanding that the Well onl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    y responded to open hands. They continued this dance for an eternity, their hands always mov) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    ing, never clutching. The Well never ran dry, for they had learned that to grasp is to lose,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (     and to relinquish is to gain everything. In the garden of trust, the harvest is infinite, b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ut in the garden of greed, the ground turns to dust.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
