BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      In the dawn of the world, two brothers, Sol and Luna, stood before the Great Well of Abund) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        ance. The Well demanded a gift to multiply its waters. Sol held five golden seeds. If he) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (         kept them, they remained mere pebbles. If he cast them into the depths, they tripled in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (         number, but he relied on Luna to share the bounty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      Sol cast his seeds into the dark water. The Well surged, returning fifteen golden grains. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        Luna, standing at the edge, faced a choice. If he walked away, he would be rich for a mo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        ment, but the Well would grow cold, and the brothers would starve in the coming winter. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        Instead, Luna scooped up the grains and returned half to Sol, honoring the cycle of grow) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        th.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      "We are but stewards of the flow," Luna whispered. Sol smiled, understanding that the Well) Tj ET
