BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      In the dawn of time, Sol held five golden seeds. He encountered Luna, a spirit of the barr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        en earth. Sol offered the seeds to her, knowing that if Luna buried them in the soil, th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        e Earth-Mother would triple their vitality.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      "If you hide them," Sol warned, "they remain stagnant. If you nurture them, they will bloo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        m into a forest.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      Luna understood the covenant. She received the seeds, and beneath her touch, they surged i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        nto a thicket of shimmering boughs. Had she been greedy, she might have consumed the har) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        vest alone, hoarding the fruit for a singular winter. But she knew the cycle of reciproc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        ity. She returned a bountiful harvest to Sol, ensuring that his storehouse was full for ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        the coming cold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      The forest grew stronger with every exchange, a testament to the trust between them. When ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        the spirits chose to hoard, the land withered, the trees grew brittle and grey. But when) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (         they shared, the bounty multiplied, turning the desert into a paradise. Thus, the law o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        f the harvest was written: to grow, one must give, and to receive, one must return. In t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        his cycle, the prosperity of the one is bound to the kindness of the other, forever entw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        ined.) Tj ET
