BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      In the dawn of the world, two brothers, Sol and Luna, stood before the Great Well of Abund) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        ance. The Well demanded a gift to multiply its waters. Sol held five golden seeds. If he) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (         kept them, they remained mere pebbles. If he cast them into the depths, they tripled in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         number, but he relied on Luna to share the bounty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      Sol cast his seeds into the dark water. The Well surged, returning fifteen golden grains. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        Luna, standing at the edge, faced a choice. If he walked away, he would be rich for a mo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ment, but the Well would grow cold, and the brothers would starve in the coming winter. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        Instead, Luna scooped up the grains and returned half to Sol, honoring the cycle of grow) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        th.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      "We are but stewards of the flow," Luna whispered. Sol smiled, understanding that the Well) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (         only responded to open hands. They continued this dance for an eternity, their hands al) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        ways moving, never clutching. The Well never ran dry, for they had learned that to grasp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (         is to lose, and to relinquish is to gain everything. In the garden of trust, the harves) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        t is infinite, but in the garden of greed, the ground turns to dust.) Tj ET
