BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        vest alone, hoarding the fruit for a singular winter. But she knew the cycle of reciproc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        ity. She returned a bountiful harvest to Sol, ensuring that his storehouse was full for ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        the coming cold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      The forest grew stronger with every exchange, a testament to the trust between them. When ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        the spirits chose to hoard, the land withered, the trees grew brittle and grey. But when) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (         they shared, the bounty multiplied, turning the desert into a paradise. Thus, the law o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        f the harvest was written: to grow, one must give, and to receive, one must return. In t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        his cycle, the prosperity of the one is bound to the kindness of the other, forever entw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        ined.) Tj ET
