BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      he mechanism of the universe triples their strength, casting fifteen shimmering strands in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      to the hands of a waiting partner. This partner, acting as the second weaver, stands at th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      e opposite end of the loom. They hold the power to either snap the threads in a fit of ind) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ividual greed or to weave them into a pattern of mutual beauty. By returning exactly half-) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      seven and a half strands-the weavers ensure the tapestry remains perfectly symmetrical and) Tj ET
